  "rules": [
    "Terrain topology is shared policy; source pixels remain owned by one explicit style-pack lane.",
    "A pure V7 lane may use only content/assets/lpc/source/lpc-terrains-v7 and V7-derived generated outputs.",
    "A pure ElizaWy lane may use only the pinned ElizaWy source mount and ElizaWy-derived generated outputs.",
    "The current mainland runtime is classified as legacy mixed until the ElizaWy mainland style pack receives its own complete transition mapping.",
    "No family whose id or stylePackLane identifies V7 may reference ElizaWy, lpc_revised, terrain_summer, cliff_summer, or common_base_terrain_32.",
    "Unsupported contacts are normalized by world generation; renderers do not borrow pixels from another style pack.",
    "V7 Rock, Stone, Mudstone, Earth, Hole, Snow, Ice, Lava, and Water families are surface materials, not structural vertical cliff faces.",
    "TileKind::Cliff is derived from elevation and exposed-neighbor topology and is never a normal ground brush.",
    "Every style pack declares separate ground-material and structural-cliff providers.",
    "A normalized runtime atlas may repack exact source cells, but it does not create cross-style transition artwork.",
    "Decorative fill variants are suppressed beside material boundaries; multi-cell details place atomically or not at all.",
    "V7 water depth uses the authored three-tier sequence Shallows -> Water -> Water_Deep; a one-cell medium-water presentation rim is derived on the deep side without changing freshwater or ocean gameplay identity.",
    "Pass167Z81 closes Gravel, Rock Ground and Mud as normal V7 ground materials using exact tuples first and reviewed V7-only connector tuples only when the direct two-material pair is absent.",
    "WateredSoil is a farming moisture state created by watering TilledSoil and is not a direct ground brush."
  ],
